 ],
 "section_summary": "This section contains a statistical roster of Japanese educational institutions located in Osaka Prefecture as of 1946, compiled under Allied occupation. It covers village and town schools—encompassing agricultural, vocational, youth, and elementary schools, as well as municipal nurse training facilities and kindergartens—alongside private institutions ranging from universities, university preparatory courses, and specialized colleges to middle schools, commercial and industrial schools, and girls' high schools. Each entry provides the institution's name, administrative location, founding date, male and female enrollment figures, and counts of full-time and part-time teachers as of April 30 and November 30, 1946.",
